201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 130 0 R
/T (Founded in 2017 by a group of lawyers and academics with expertise in refugee, human rights and migration law, NANSEN aims to develop and make available high-quality legal assistance for people in need of international protection and people affected by statelessness, contributing to the effective protection of their fundamental rights.)
/E (Founded in 2017 by a group of lawyers and academics with expertise in refugee, human rights and migration law, NANSEN aims to develop and make available high-quality legal assistance for people in need of international protection and people affected by statelessness, contributing to the effective protection of their fundamental rights.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 130 0 R
/T (The need for this work remains clear. In 2025, 34,439 people applied for international protection in Belgium.1 Behind each application is a person navigating a legal and administrative system that can be difficult to understand, increasingly complex and constantly evolving. At the same time, the political and public space for a welcoming and human-centred approach to international protection is shrinking. These procedures come on top of the everyday challenges faced by persons forced to flee, including the many forms of trauma that displacement may entail.  People affected by statelessness face distinct, but equally significant, challenges in establishing their status, accessing protection and a durable residency status, and enjoying their rights. )
/E (The need for this work remains clear. In 2025, 34,439 people applied for international protection in Belgium.1 Behind each application is a person navigating a legal and administrative system that can be difficult to understand, increasingly complex and constantly evolving. At the same time, the political and public space for a welcoming and human-centred approach to international protection is shrinking. These procedures come on top of the everyday challenges faced by persons forced to flee, including the many forms of trauma that displacement may entail.  People affected by statelessness face distinct, but equally significant, challenges in establishing their status, accessing protection and a durable residency status, and enjoying their rights. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3 5 4]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 130 0 R
/T (As a centre of legal expertise on international protection and statelessness, NANSEN works to ensure that quality legal assistance reaches the people who need it most. We look closely at each person's situation, recognising that everyone may experience visible or less visible vulnerabilities, and draw on an interdisciplinary approach to understand and dismantle the barriers they face.)
/E (As a centre of legal expertise on international protection and statelessness, NANSEN works to ensure that quality legal assistance reaches the people who need it most. We look closely at each person's situation, recognising that everyone may experience visible or less visible vulnerabilities, and draw on an interdisciplinary approach to understand and dismantle the barriers they face.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
