221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (In 2025, our small but dedicated team continued to advance this work across all three objectives. This report tells that story in two ways.  One that focuses on how and what we work on, such as administrative detention, sexual orientation and/or gender identity, statelessness, and survivors of torture. The second highlights our own individual casework, where NANSEN's legal expertise helps safeguard people's rights and contributes to the development of legal practice on the ground.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (These two stories are never truly separate. What we learn from individual cases sharpens our legal analysis; what we develop through our thematic work - tools, training, recommendations - strengthens the support available to others facing similar barriers. Together, they capture how NANSEN works: grounding legal and interdisciplinary expertise in practice, and building expertise from practice, to make international protection and statelessness procedures fairer and fundamental rights more accessible.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
