/P 133 0 R
/E (Said \(alias\) comes from Afghanistan. Because of the risks he would face if returned to that country, Italy granted him subsidiary protection. In 2025, Said travelled to Belgium. Arriving from Turkey, he was arrested at the Belgian border and placed in detention. Belgian authorities were planning to send him back to Turkey. Made aware of the upcoming flight, NANSEN wrote an intervention to warn the authorities of the significant risk of indirect refoulement and prevent them from sending Said to Turkey.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
