263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (People seeking international protection because of their sexual orientation and/or gender identity \(SOGI\) face multiple and intersecting forms of exclusion and discrimination. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (Within the asylum procedure, credibility assessments can be particularly challenging for SOGI applicants, who are often required to substantiate deeply personal feelings and experiences within a system that is not always equipped to understand them. Outside the asylum procedure, discrimination, stigma and even violence can follow them into their communities, reception centres and support services. Adding to these challenges, relevant expertise is scattered across different organisations, making support difficult to navigate.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (NANSEN responds by pairing its legal expertise with organisations working directly with LGBTQIA+ people. WAWY \("We Are With You"\) is central to this: a network we run alongside Merhaba, the Rainbow Refugee Committee, Vluchtelingenwerk Vlaanderen and the Humanitarian Hub. With financial support from Equal.brussels, WAWY brings these organisations together to strengthen collaboration, exchange expertise and improve support for SOGI applicants. Through regular partner meetings, joint training, case discussions, field visits and a bi-monthly newsletter, we bring legal expertise and an interdisciplinary approach to the table and translate practical, on-the-ground knowledge and lived experiences shared by the network back into our own casework. The number of SOGI cases that NANSEN assisted in recent years has grown steadily - a sign both of rising need and of the value of these partnerships and referral pathways.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3 448 0 R 5 449 0 R 7]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Span
/K [4]
/Pg 17 0 R
/P 448 0 R
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Span
/K [6]
/Pg 17 0 R
/P 449 0 R
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (In 2025, we turned casework and collaboration into tools for practitioners. We developed two practical fact sheets available in Dutch, French and English - one providing a step-by-step overview of the Belgian asylum procedure, with specific points of attention for SOGI applicants and the other focusing on evidence and the challenges these applicants may face when substantiating their request for international protection.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8 450 0 R 10 451 0 R 12]
>>
endobj
