282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (Omar \(alias\), an Iraqi man, was referred to NANSEN by Merhaba for legal assistance with his seventh application for international protection, the first based on his sexual orientation. He had fled Iraq because of his homosexuality but had not disclosed this during his previous applications. NANSEN assessed that his sexual orientation constituted a new element that could significantly increase the likelihood of establishing his need for international protection. NANSEN therefore formally intervened before the CGRS and documented the reasons why he had not disclosed his sexual orientation in the past: shame, fear of the Belgian authorities, his life in a reception centre with many Iraqi residents and concerns about the Iraqi interpreter during his first interview. NANSEN further highlighted his particular vulnerability. Omar was subsequently invited to a personal interview, which NANSEN attended as his trusted person. Omar was later recognised as a refugee.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
