/P 136 0 R
/E (We also went further: together with other organisations, NANSEN challenged parts of the new procedure before the Constitutional Court, arguing that certain provisions created disproportionate barriers to residence, provided insufficient procedural safeguards, and failed to meet Belgium's obligations under the 1954 Convention relating to the Status of Stateless Persons. The Court delivered its judgment in 2026, annulling several provisions of the law and NANSEN will continue to monitor its implications for stateless people trying to access residence.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8 455 0 R 10]
>>
