/P 140 0 R
/E (We translate this monitoring into practical tools, legal analysis and knowledge-sharing, responding to emerging trends. In 2025, this included a note on people with international protection status in Greece who subsequently seek protection in Belgium. The note responded to a practical need: understanding when a person who has already received international protection in Greece may nevertheless have grounds to seek international protection in Belgium. NANSEN brought together recent information on the situation of beneficiaries of international protection in Greece and jurisprudence of the Council for Alien Law Litigation \(Dutch Chamber\). It provides practitioners with a tool for supporting people who may find themselves in this situation.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2 463 0 R 4]
>>
