/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (In 2025, NANSEN worked actively on 171 individual cases. The number is modest; the work behind it is not. Each case can mean weeks of reading through administrative files and decisions, researching country-of-origin information, meeting with the person , coordinating with their lawyers, psychologists, doctors, social workers or the wider support network around them.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (The majority concerned people seeking international protection on the Belgian territory \(83 cases\) or while held in administrative detention \(74 cases\). 14 cases concerned questions of stateless persons, or children at risk of statelessness. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (Palestinian applicants were the most represented, followed by people from Afghanistan, Yemen, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Guinea and Syria. NANSEN supported 101 men, 51 women and 19 families.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
