1540 0 obj
<<
/Title (Since 2023, troubling emerging practices related to the prevention of statelessness under Article 10 of the Belgian Nationality Code for children born in Belgium have been observed. These developments particularly concerned children born in Belgium to parents of Palestinian origin and, in 2025, resulted in important case law. NANSEN continues to monitor these developments and provides legal support to lawyers and through individual casework.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1542 0 R
/Next 1538 0 R
>>
endobj
1541 0 obj
<<
/Title (A significant new step in 2025: NANSEN held its first-ever dedicated meeting on gender with the Office of the Commissioner General for Refugees and Stateless Persons \(CGRS\) Gender service. We shared our findings on emerging challenges in SOGI-related cases, highlighted barriers and presented our expertise and concrete recommendations.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1539 0 R
/Next 1543 0 R
>>
endobj
1542 0 obj
<<
/Title (The complexity of the legal framework also creates a need for accessible and reliable information for practitioners. NANSEN produced a practical guide on statelessness in Belgium, bringing together the legal and practical information practitioners need most. Publication of the guide was put on hold pending the Constitutional Court proceedings, as the outcome could affect the applicable legal framework. While the guide will be updated following the Constitutional Court judgment and any relevant changes to the procedures, NANSEN continues to use the guide in its daily work supporting affected individuals.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1544 0 R
/Next 1540 0 R
>>
endobj
1543 0 obj
<<
/Title (The result of all this work: practitioners with sharper tools, applicants with clearer guidance and better support, and a growing body of evidence pointing to where change is still needed.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1541 0 R
/Next 1544 0 R
>>
endobj
